---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About | RealSalaryCheck">
  <main class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 md:py-24 animate-fade-in">
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black tracking-tight mb-4" style="color: var(--logo-primary)">About RealSalaryCheck</h1>
      <p class="text-sm md:text-base font-medium leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--nav-text)">
        Bridging the gap between gross numbers and actual lifestyle realities for global professionals.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 space-y-8 shadow-xl" style="background-color: var(--card-bg); border: 1px solid var(--card-border);">
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold" style="color: var(--logo-primary)">Our Mission</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--nav-text)">
          When professionals evaluate international or out-of-state job opportunities, standard nominal exchange rates often obscure the real economic picture. RealSalaryCheck was built to instantly resolve this fragmentation by evaluating financial purchasing power through normalized macroeconomic indices.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold" style="color: var(--logo-primary)">How It Works</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--nav-text)">
          The application leverages current regional Purchasing Power Parity (PPP) conversion vectors. By stripping away arbitrary base currency rates, the computation models what an offered foreign compensation structure actually delivers relative to your local day-to-day cost of living.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold" style="color: var(--logo-primary)">Data Integrity</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--nav-text)">
          Our internal models utilize benchmarks compiled from standardized global economic databases, updated periodically to ensure structural reliability. Calculations operate exclusively client-side to maximize execution speed and verify parameters with minimal latency.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout> 